Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Fiber Bundles", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell["\<\
A fibered graph is an inert total graph with a vertex projection. Its base is \
reconstructed from that projection and its total edges. General operations \
generate examples, extend sections, choose complete connections and read \
transport and monodromy. Graph bundles additionally require a common fiber \
graph and transverse matchings preserving fiber adjacency. Particular tangent \
and metric-selected models are Experimental constructions within this \
category.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

